To design the goal model for the multi-robot system mission, we break down the mission into phases and tasks, considering parallel and sequential execution, and fallback mechanisms for task handover. Here's the structured goal model:

### Goal Model Structure

**Top-Level Goal:**
- **G1: Successfully complete the collection and delivery mission.**
  - **Type:** Achieve
  - **Target Condition:** The mission is successfully completed with all resources collected and delivered.
  - **Relation:** AND (G2 and G3 must both be completed)
  - **Justification:** The mission requires both collection and delivery phases to be successful.

**Sub-Goals:**
- **G2: Collect resources from specified storage locations.**
  - **Type:** Achieve
  - **Target Condition:** All required resources are collected from their respective storage locations.
  - **Relation:** AND (All subgoals under G2 must be completed)
  - **Justification:** All resources must be collected before delivery can begin.

  - **G2.1: Collect resources from Storage Location A.**
    - **Type:** Achieve
    - **Target Condition:** Resources from Storage Location A are collected.
    - **Relation:** OR (Multiple robots can collect from different storages in parallel)
    - **Justification:** Each storage can be handled independently, allowing parallel execution.

  - **G2.2: Collect resources from Storage Location B.**
    - **Type:** Achieve
    - **Target Condition:** Resources from Storage Location B are collected.
    - **Relation:** OR (Multiple robots can collect from different storages in parallel)
    - **Justification:** Each storage can be handled independently, allowing parallel execution.

  - **... (Additional G2.x for other storage locations)**

- **G3: Deliver collected resources to the specified location.**
  - **Type:** Achieve
  - **Target Condition:** All collected resources are delivered to the specified location.
  - **Relation:** AND (All delivery tasks must be completed)
  - **Justification:** The delivery phase requires multiple runs to transport all resources.

  - **AT3.1: Deliver resources to Delivery Location.**
    - **Type:** Perform
    - **Text:** Deliver a portion of the collected resources to the specified location.
    - **Relation:** Sequential execution (Each delivery run is dependent on the previous)
    - **Location:** Delivery Location
    - **Number of Robots:** 1
    - **Justification:** Each delivery run must be completed before the next can begin.

  - **AT3.2: Deliver next portion of resources to Delivery Location.**
    - **Type:** Perform
    - **Text:** Deliver the next portion of collected resources to the specified location.
    - **Relation:** Sequential execution
    - **Location:** Delivery Location
    - **Number of Robots:** 1
    - **Justification:** Each delivery run is sequential.

  - **... (Additional AT3.x for other delivery runs)**

### Task Details:
- **Task Nodes:**
  - **AT2.1: CollectResourcesFromStorageA**
    - **Location:** Storage Location A
    - **Number of Robots:** 1
    - **Justification:** One robot per storage location to avoid interference.

  - **AT2.2: CollectResourcesFromStorageB**
    - **Location:** Storage Location B
    - **Number of Robots:** 1
    - **Justification:** One robot per storage location.

  - **AT3.1: DeliverResourcesToDestination**
    - **Location:** Delivery Location
    - **Number of Robots:** 1
    - **Justification:** Sequential delivery requires one robot per run.

### Summary Table

| Goal ID | Goal Title | Goal Type | Target Condition | Relation | Justification |
|--------|------------|-----------|------------------|----------|----------------|
| G1     | Complete Mission | Achieve | Mission completed | AND (G2, G3) | Both phases must succeed. |
| G2     | Collect Resources | Achieve | All resources collected | AND (G2.1, G2.2, ...) | All resources must be collected. |
| G2.1   | Collect from A | Achieve | Resources from A collected | OR (parallel) | Independent storage collection. |
| G3     | Deliver Resources | Achieve | All delivered | AND (AT3.1, AT3.2, ...) | All delivery runs must complete. |
| AT3.1  | Deliver Run 1 | Perform | Resources delivered | Sequential | Each run depends on the previous. |

### Relationships:
- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND]**
  - **Justification:** Both collection and delivery are necessary for mission success.
- **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2, ... [AND]**
  - **Justification:** All resources must be collected.
- **G2.1 -> AT2.1 [OR]**
  - **Justification:** Independent collection from each storage.
- **G3 -> AT3.1, AT3.2, ... [AND]**
  - **Justification:** All delivery runs must be completed.

This model ensures efficient execution of the mission by leveraging parallel collection and sequential delivery, with fallback mechanisms to handle battery issues and task handover.
